.TH HELLO 1 "2024-01-15" "MPC v0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
hello \- print a greeting message
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B hello
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.RI [ name ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
The
.B hello
utility prints a friendly greeting message to standard output.
If a name is provided as an argument, it greets that person specifically.
Otherwise, it prints a generic greeting to the world.
.PP
The greeting is always followed by a newline character.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Display help information and exit.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version
Display version information and exit.
.TP
.BR \-u ", " \-\-uppercase
Print the greeting in uppercase letters.
.SH EXAMPLES
Print a generic greeting:
.nf
.RS
$ hello
Hello, World!
.RE
.fi
.PP
Greet a specific person:
.nf
.RS
$ hello Alice
Hello, Alice!
.RE
.fi
.PP
Greet in uppercase:
.nf
.RS
$ hello --uppercase Bob
HELLO, BOB!
.RE
.fi
.SH EXIT STATUS
.B hello
exits 0 on success, and >0 if an error occurs.
